Upstream-Status: Not-applicable
Exit: Drop when GNOME's synced 0001-project.conf-Add-GNOME-CAS-servers.patch carries the Bluefin CAS, or Bluefin stops serving FSDK artifacts.
Subject: project.conf: Add Bluefin CAS server

Add https://cache.projectbluefin.io:11001 to the junctioned FSDK's
artifacts and source-caches, after gbm.gnome.org, so junction elements
pull from the Bluefin CAS without per-user BuildStream config. The
top-level project.conf remotes do not reach junction elements.

Keep this in Dakota's patch queue: patches/freedesktop-sdk is
overwritten by `just patch-sync` and checked by `just patch-drift-check`.
Applies on top of patches/freedesktop-sdk/0001.

Mirrors projectbluefin/server#400.

diff --git a/project.conf b/project.conf
index 982bddf..ff7c2bc 100644
--- a/project.conf
+++ b/project.conf
@@ -155,6 +155,12 @@ artifacts:
     retry-limit: 4
     retry-delay: 500
     request-timeout: 300
+- url: https://cache.projectbluefin.io:11001
+  connection-config:
+    keepalive-time: 60
+    retry-limit: 4
+    retry-delay: 500
+    request-timeout: 300
 
 source-caches:
 - url: https://cache.freedesktop-sdk.io:11001
@@ -169,6 +175,12 @@ source-caches:
     retry-limit: 4
     retry-delay: 500
     request-timeout: 300
+- url: https://cache.projectbluefin.io:11001
+  connection-config:
+    keepalive-time: 60
+    retry-limit: 4
+    retry-delay: 500
+    request-timeout: 300
 
 sandbox:
   build-arch: '%{target_arch}'
